<Layout title="About this starter" description="Learn how this Astro directory example is structured and explore its real-world editorial references.">
<article class="prose"><p class="eyebrow">FROM IDEA TO DIRECTORY</p><h1>A useful starting point.</h1><p>This is a working example for developers building a tool directory with Astro. It includes typed metadata, static pagination, category pages, client-side search, and individual tool pages.</p><h2>Real-world references</h2><p>This starter’s author also maintains <a href="https://navsprout.com/">NavSprout</a>, a curated directory of useful websites and online tools, and <a href="https://ainavly.com/">AINavly</a>, covering AI tools, creative applications, web projects, and browser games.</p><p>These projects provide editorial context for the example. This starter is not their production source code, and the sample entries are not sponsored placements.</p><h2>Make it your own</h2><p>Edit <code>src/data/tools.ts</code> to add resources. Update the site URL, branding, and descriptions before deploying. The repository documentation explains routing, search, metadata, and Cloudflare Pages deployment.</p><a class="button" href="https://github.com/limeng05/astro-directory-starter">Read the documentation ↗</a></article>
</Layout>
